244	        // This gate is advisory, not a decode-capacity reservation. Normal
245	        // decode routing books scheduler state before returning a routing
246	        // decision; conditional-disagg is still deciding whether to enter that
247	        // decode path, so booking here would double-count unless we added a
248	        // reservation handoff to the downstream decode router. Use the selected
249	        // worker's projected decode load, including this request, but allow for
250	        // concurrent bypass decisions to race the same threshold.
251	        let decode_gate_configured = self.conditional_disagg_decode_busy_threshold.is_some();
252	        let decode_busy = if policy_says_bypass {
